{"body":{"asks":"Two copies of a holon come apart only when a commit lands in some stores it touches and misses others, which the engine sees as it lands. Where is the holon then marked diverged, and by whom: in the stores that took the commit, by the engine while it lives, or both; how is the later commit's version found to answer; and once that is built, may a read ask for a holon only where holding says it lies, rather than every store? Until it is answered a read asks every store for every holon, so divergence is never silent.","awaits":true,"raised":[{"$ref":"1M7K3256Z8HP0XS"}],"stands":"open","touches":[{"$ref":"1M7JND1XQPFA08T"}]},"id":"1M7K32QVB6KW000","instance":["1M6YBY3G000001E"],"name":"Where divergence is marked","prev":null}
